{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Laila writes a list of numbers. Her first number is 4. Each number after the first is 7 more than the previous number. Which of the following numbers appears in Laila's list?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1df4ffe2b3a3428e8b4a01daf2467846af0cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 45 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 46 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 47 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 48 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the numbers in the list until we get one of the answer choices:\n</p><p>The second term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503e59bd9d8bfebfc24689bc7eae5aa624350287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 7 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb26d47a2a7aa282b6ef5751f1d9ade1e5647c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 7 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The fourth term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/4066654033050c12ab40d55ba25da45dc7d52d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 7 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The fifth term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b8f224c663f4c6023d5683bdf5c3a2ce8ee50ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 7 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The sixth term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84a81edfc7c5efaca26caaf321a3b09ba78da51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 + 7 = 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The seventh term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a80f5b1e7ad51779085f8558d84f397a4b919cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 + 7 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 46}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that each number in the list would be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74cc07a08223f97a228c9957467f9e3f3260266c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, because the list starts out with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and each term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than the first term. This means that our answer choice would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7d0180596b39f078b9ccc750bff09efea4c0df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 6 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90cc27affd59f059f5a536bdf40e6d366ae23f22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 7 = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> (around all the answer choices), so we can see that the only answer choice that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c4d840092644a4fde70f48293cab216792e7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 46}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/